WEBVTT

00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:12.130
Can you imagine...

00:00:12.130 --> 00:00:17.470
...a life in which you could never
touch the one you love?

00:00:17.470 --> 00:00:20.310
He takes the life of whatever he touches.

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:23.770
That was the curse the witch put on him.

00:00:23.770 --> 00:00:28.060
Plants, animals... and people
are no exception, of course.

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:31.480
Regarding her son, doomed to live his life
without knowing the warmth of another,

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:34.150
his mother only complained.

00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:36.660
"That child is like Death incarnate..."

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:37.660
she said.

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:43.750
I'm actually going to meet Mother?

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:47.710
Good morning, Your Grace.

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:48.710
Alice.

00:00:52.130 --> 00:00:53.590
Good morning.

00:00:53.590 --> 00:00:56.760
Today's the day you go
to the main residence.

00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:58.680
How are you feeling?

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:00.140
Not so good.

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:03.810
I haven't even broken my curse yet, so I
don't know what she's going to say.

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:05.850
Everything will be fine.

00:01:05.850 --> 00:01:07.560
Your Grace?

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:09.270
Cheer up, now.

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:12.980
You're a bit too close, as usual.

00:02:43.030 --> 00:02:46.200
"Episode 12: Together with the Duke..."

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:48.790
I'm feeling a little anxious.

00:02:48.790 --> 00:02:51.040
You see, this has never happened before.

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:54.630
I've always let Rob handle the
correspondence with the main residence.

00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:57.210
And did you let him handle going
to the main residence, as well?

00:02:57.210 --> 00:03:00.430
Yeah. It'll be my first time going there
since coming to live here.

00:03:00.430 --> 00:03:03.300
I haven't seen Mother since I was a kid.

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:07.810
I may be scared, but that doesn't
mean I don't want to see her.

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:09.100
I know what you mean.

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:10.190
But...

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:16.270
...the truth is...

00:03:16.270 --> 00:03:20.150
...the truth is I wanted to see her
after I'd broken my curse.

00:03:20.150 --> 00:03:24.660
It pains me for her to think that
nothing has changed since then.

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:25.660
Your Grace...

00:03:36.210 --> 00:03:39.130
Looks like it's going to snow again.

00:03:39.130 --> 00:03:40.300
You're right.

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:45.220
I wonder if the carriage that's
coming to get me will be all right.

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:46.720
Your Grace?

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:50.810
Would you mind if I went along
with you to the main residence?

00:03:50.810 --> 00:03:51.890
You? Come with me?

00:03:52.770 --> 00:03:53.850
Alice...

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:04.160
Sure enough, it's started snowing.

00:04:05.570 --> 00:04:09.700
I wish it would snow hard
enough to cancel this trip.

00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:13.920
I'll go make you some more tea.

00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:20.630
My love for Alice hasn't changed.

00:04:20.630 --> 00:04:24.760
When I see Mother, I'll tell her about us.

00:04:24.760 --> 00:04:26.930
And maybe, one day...

00:04:30.020 --> 00:04:33.560
He's gone over to his family's place?
That's surprising.

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:37.270
Yeah, and Alice is gone, too.

00:04:37.270 --> 00:04:39.440
Why did I bother coming here?

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:41.280
Please accept my apologies.

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:43.280
--That was close!
--However, this is a trial...

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:44.490
Whoa!

00:04:44.490 --> 00:04:48.700
...that His Grace, or rather,
the two of them...

00:04:48.700 --> 00:04:51.790
...must one day overcome.

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:07.260
What do you remember
about your family's estate?

00:05:07.260 --> 00:05:11.600
My only memories are of playing
the piano or horsing around.

00:05:12.390 --> 00:05:13.850
What about you?

00:05:13.850 --> 00:05:16.020
I only remember you, Your Grace.

00:05:30.490 --> 00:05:33.330
It certainly is a beautiful place.

00:05:36.790 --> 00:05:39.000
You finally made it.

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:41.840
And sure enough, Alice came with you.

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:43.670
You certainly took your
sweet time getting here.

00:05:43.670 --> 00:05:46.840
Sorry. We had to wait out the snowstorm...

00:05:46.840 --> 00:05:48.550
What did Mother have to say?

00:05:48.550 --> 00:05:50.180
Nothing, really.

00:05:50.180 --> 00:05:53.140
She just said you should see her
as soon as you get here.

00:05:53.140 --> 00:05:54.770
You and you alone, Dearest Brother.

00:05:54.770 --> 00:05:57.020
Me alone?

00:05:57.020 --> 00:06:01.230
I'm going to say hello
to all of the servants.

00:06:01.230 --> 00:06:02.820
Yeah, you should.

00:06:02.820 --> 00:06:06.650
I told the maids that you'd
probably be coming, Alice.

00:06:06.650 --> 00:06:08.450
Thank you, Lady Viola.

00:06:08.450 --> 00:06:11.370
All right, Your Grace, I'll see you later.

00:06:12.580 --> 00:06:14.290
Good luck, Your Grace.

00:06:14.290 --> 00:06:16.000
Oh, you're leaving me?

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:19.420
Alice! Oh, my adorable Alice!

00:06:19.420 --> 00:06:21.250
Gawd, you're so annoying!

00:06:37.140 --> 00:06:39.020
We're here.

00:06:39.020 --> 00:06:40.400
This is Mother's room.

00:06:43.480 --> 00:06:45.530
I've got something to tell you.

00:06:45.530 --> 00:06:46.860
Wh-What is it?

00:06:46.860 --> 00:06:51.450
I'm the one who blabbed to Mother
that Viola had been going to the villa.

00:06:51.450 --> 00:06:54.330
That's probably the reason why
she called you here today.

00:06:54.330 --> 00:06:56.200
Hey, don't worry about it.

00:06:56.200 --> 00:06:58.040
You're quite a gentleman, Walter.

00:06:58.040 --> 00:07:00.080
You've got no business
giving me compliments!

00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:01.170
S-S-Sorry.

00:07:01.170 --> 00:07:03.790
Gawd, you're <i>both </i>annoying!

00:07:03.790 --> 00:07:06.250
Anyway, go in and see her,
Dearest Brother.

00:07:06.250 --> 00:07:08.970
We'll be here waiting for you.

00:07:08.970 --> 00:07:10.220
O-Okay.

00:07:12.340 --> 00:07:13.470
Come in.

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:16.180
I hope I'm not disturbing you.

00:07:24.310 --> 00:07:25.900
Mother...

00:07:25.900 --> 00:07:27.690
It's been a long time, hasn't it?

00:07:27.690 --> 00:07:29.610
I-It certainly has.

00:07:33.070 --> 00:07:38.080
It's been over ten years since you were
cursed, and you still haven't broken it?

00:07:38.080 --> 00:07:39.370
Forgive me.

00:07:39.370 --> 00:07:42.420
It looks like it may
t-take a little longer.

00:07:42.420 --> 00:07:45.290
It's already late,
so we'll speak tomorrow.

00:07:45.290 --> 00:07:47.050
You may stay here tonight.

00:07:47.050 --> 00:07:48.130
A-All right.

00:07:48.130 --> 00:07:50.340
Um, and...

00:07:50.340 --> 00:07:51.970
...there's something I'd like to tell you.

00:07:51.970 --> 00:07:53.640
Didn't you hear me?

00:07:53.640 --> 00:07:56.010
We'll speak tomorrow.

00:07:56.010 --> 00:07:57.390
Forgive me.

00:07:57.390 --> 00:07:58.560
Good night.

00:08:07.230 --> 00:08:08.610
Good job!

00:08:08.610 --> 00:08:11.320
Mother was feeling kind today.

00:08:11.320 --> 00:08:13.070
--Yeah.
--That was her being kind?!

00:08:13.070 --> 00:08:16.950
You're too used to Rob and Alice's
kindness, Dearest Brother.

00:08:16.950 --> 00:08:20.120
That's the trouble with you
being brought up at the villa.

00:08:20.120 --> 00:08:21.710
We'll take you to the guest room.

00:08:26.330 --> 00:08:28.550
I couldn't talk to Mother at all.

00:08:30.130 --> 00:08:33.340
I wonder how Alice is doing.

00:08:33.340 --> 00:08:37.140
Oh, my! Alice, look how much you've grown!

00:08:37.140 --> 00:08:39.560
You're a beauty, just like Sharon was.

00:08:39.560 --> 00:08:41.930
And that skin tone!
I'd expect nothing less.

00:08:41.930 --> 00:08:44.730
Th-Thank you.

00:08:44.730 --> 00:08:47.020
After Sharon passed away and...

00:08:47.020 --> 00:08:49.860
...you were taken in by your relatives,

00:08:49.860 --> 00:08:54.320
I constantly worried about
how you were getting on.

00:08:54.320 --> 00:08:59.490
I am so sorry I couldn't
do anything for you then.

00:08:59.490 --> 00:09:00.790
Oh, I see.

00:09:01.910 --> 00:09:04.290
My sweet Alice,

00:09:04.290 --> 00:09:07.380
I'll protect you no matter what.

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:08.630
I love you!

00:09:12.460 --> 00:09:14.840
You're going to stay
the night, aren't you?

00:09:14.840 --> 00:09:17.260
The room that you and your
mother used back then...

00:09:17.260 --> 00:09:19.510
It's all cleaned up nice and proper.

00:09:19.510 --> 00:09:20.720
Really?

00:09:24.930 --> 00:09:25.940
Sharon?!

00:09:27.810 --> 00:09:32.280
Madam? This is Alice, Sharon's daughter.

00:09:32.280 --> 00:09:34.110
O-Oh...

00:09:34.110 --> 00:09:37.660
...I see. You're the maid from the villa.

00:09:37.660 --> 00:09:40.780
Your black outfit looks like hers, so I...

00:09:40.780 --> 00:09:42.490
Please forget about this.

00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:48.380
The lady of the house and
Sharon were very close.

00:09:48.380 --> 00:09:53.000
They were both so cheerful. They were
close in age and shared common interests.

00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:55.380
But after Sharon passed away,

00:09:55.380 --> 00:09:58.970
the lady of the house started
acting a bit differently.

00:10:00.010 --> 00:10:03.220
Oh, I see.

00:10:03.220 --> 00:10:05.430
My sweet Alice,

00:10:05.430 --> 00:10:06.560
I love you!

00:10:08.650 --> 00:10:09.650
Yes?

00:10:11.730 --> 00:10:12.610
Hey there...

00:10:12.610 --> 00:10:14.230
Oh, it's you, Your Grace.

00:10:14.230 --> 00:10:16.610
I came to see you.

00:10:16.610 --> 00:10:18.320
How did things go?

00:10:18.320 --> 00:10:21.410
Did the other servants
give you a hard time?

00:10:21.410 --> 00:10:23.950
No, actually they treated me rather well.

00:10:23.950 --> 00:10:26.330
They're all such friendly people.

00:10:26.330 --> 00:10:28.040
Well, I'm glad to hear that.

00:10:28.040 --> 00:10:31.250
What about you, Your Grace?

00:10:31.250 --> 00:10:36.300
We only spoke very briefly,
but Mother hadn't changed at all.

00:10:36.300 --> 00:10:39.300
She said we'd talk tomorrow
because it was so late.

00:10:39.300 --> 00:10:42.010
So, you were able to speak
with her normally, then.

00:10:42.010 --> 00:10:44.180
Well, yeah, I guess.

00:10:44.180 --> 00:10:47.680
That's great. It makes me so happy.

00:10:49.440 --> 00:10:53.060
I know we've only been
apart for a few hours,

00:10:53.060 --> 00:10:55.030
but I just wanted to see you so much.

00:10:56.740 --> 00:10:58.740
What would you do...

00:10:58.740 --> 00:11:00.490
...if I told you I did, too?

00:11:00.490 --> 00:11:01.950
She's so adorable...

00:11:01.950 --> 00:11:03.490
Really, really adorable!

00:11:03.490 --> 00:11:05.910
My love for her grows with
every passing second.

00:11:07.410 --> 00:11:08.910
No!

00:11:08.910 --> 00:11:09.750
I can't handle this!

00:11:09.750 --> 00:11:11.960
After being apart from Alice for just a
few hours, she is simply too adorable!

00:11:11.960 --> 00:11:16.000
I don't think my sanity can
hold out much longer!

00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:17.460
I think I'm going to hit the hay.

00:11:17.460 --> 00:11:22.590
Tomorrow Viola's going to take me
to the place where I was cursed.

00:11:22.590 --> 00:11:24.510
Oh, really?

00:11:25.720 --> 00:11:27.100
Good night, Alice.

00:11:27.100 --> 00:11:28.810
I'm glad we could talk.

00:11:28.810 --> 00:11:30.810
Good night, Your Grace.

00:11:44.870 --> 00:11:47.240
I wish we could've spent
a little more time together...

00:11:57.710 --> 00:12:00.840
So, what's it like being
back here after all this time?

00:12:01.760 --> 00:12:04.010
Do you remember anything?

00:12:04.010 --> 00:12:05.640
Only bits and pieces.

00:12:05.640 --> 00:12:09.220
I'm not trying to be rude here, but I find
the place is smaller than I remember.

00:12:09.220 --> 00:12:13.100
When I was a kid,
it just seemed a lot bigger...

00:12:13.100 --> 00:12:17.020
Well, this place looks much
nicer than the villa does.

00:12:17.020 --> 00:12:22.450
I wonder how Rob and Alice look
after that place all by themselves.

00:12:22.450 --> 00:12:24.360
I'm really grateful to them.

00:12:24.360 --> 00:12:26.870
Okay, we're here.

00:12:26.870 --> 00:12:27.990
This is the spot, right?

00:12:31.080 --> 00:12:33.460
One of the servants
told me about it before.

00:12:33.460 --> 00:12:37.750
That you were cursed
in front of this grave.

00:12:38.920 --> 00:12:41.130
There's no doubt about it.

00:12:41.130 --> 00:12:42.130
This is the place.

00:12:43.130 --> 00:12:44.430
This is where I was...

00:12:47.050 --> 00:12:51.980
It was springtime. That day, I was by
myself, looking for a four-leaf clover.

00:12:51.980 --> 00:12:54.520
I was probably going to give it to Alice.

00:12:54.520 --> 00:12:55.940
Yeah, yeah. Then what?

00:12:57.860 --> 00:13:00.690
Suddenly, there was all this smoke,
and I couldn't see anything around me.

00:13:00.690 --> 00:13:03.360
Somebody grabbed me from behind.

00:13:03.360 --> 00:13:04.570
And then...

00:13:04.570 --> 00:13:08.660
No one shall love you,
and you shall love no one.

00:13:08.660 --> 00:13:12.040
You shall live a life of misery.

00:13:12.040 --> 00:13:15.040
...before I knew it, I'd been cursed.

00:13:15.920 --> 00:13:19.710
I'd almost forgotten about it but
coming here jogged my memory.

00:13:19.710 --> 00:13:22.960
Hmm. Don't you remember anything else?

00:13:22.960 --> 00:13:25.090
Um, also...

00:13:25.090 --> 00:13:28.600
The softness of her breasts
pressed against my back...

00:13:28.600 --> 00:13:30.930
--...and stuff.
--Whatever.

00:13:30.930 --> 00:13:36.520
But you know what I heard from Rob? He
said you didn't remember who Alice was.

00:13:36.520 --> 00:13:39.520
Why didn't you?
You've liked her since you were kids.

00:13:39.520 --> 00:13:41.480
I think it's probably because...

00:13:41.480 --> 00:13:44.030
...after I was cursed and
couldn't see her anymore,

00:13:44.030 --> 00:13:49.370
I was lonely, and the only way to forget
about it was to purge her from my memory.

00:13:49.370 --> 00:13:52.120
Hmm. Well, it's great you could
see her again, huh?

00:13:52.120 --> 00:13:54.450
--Yep!
--Oh, boy...

00:13:59.540 --> 00:14:02.210
Oh! Good morning, Mother.

00:14:03.840 --> 00:14:06.220
Viola, you're too close to him.

00:14:06.220 --> 00:14:09.340
He's dangerous, so stay
farther away from him.

00:14:09.340 --> 00:14:11.640
I see you're wearing those clothes again.

00:14:11.640 --> 00:14:15.520
It's disgraceful.
Think of how it reflects on me.

00:14:15.520 --> 00:14:17.980
I'll speak to you during dinner.

00:14:17.980 --> 00:14:19.520
Don't be late.

00:14:24.230 --> 00:14:25.280
Viola...

00:14:25.280 --> 00:14:28.360
It's all right. I'm used to it.

00:14:28.360 --> 00:14:33.200
I told you that deep down
I wanted to live at the villa.

00:14:33.200 --> 00:14:34.910
But I guess I can't.

00:14:36.290 --> 00:14:38.620
And neither can Walter.

00:14:38.620 --> 00:14:43.250
Being born into this family means
we can't live our own lives.

00:14:43.250 --> 00:14:47.880
We live comfortable lives, and our names
appear on our distinguished family tree.

00:14:47.880 --> 00:14:51.260
Oddly enough, you may be the one
who's better off, Dearest Brother.

00:14:51.260 --> 00:14:54.560
"Has anyone ever told you that
you were someone else's alternate?"

00:15:13.830 --> 00:15:16.580
What are you doing? Hurry up and sit down.

00:15:44.810 --> 00:15:46.520
What I'd like to talk about...

00:15:46.520 --> 00:15:48.820
...concerns this family.

00:15:48.820 --> 00:15:50.240
As you are aware,

00:15:50.240 --> 00:15:52.160
the present head of the family,

00:15:52.160 --> 00:15:56.280
your father has been hospitalized
for quite some time.

00:15:56.280 --> 00:16:00.910
His condition fluctuates,
and his prognosis is poor.

00:16:00.910 --> 00:16:04.000
If we wait until the worst happens
to him, it'll be too late.

00:16:04.000 --> 00:16:08.960
We must decide ahead of time whether
you or Walter shall be his heir.

00:16:08.960 --> 00:16:10.300
Do you understand?

00:16:10.300 --> 00:16:11.880
Yes, I do.

00:16:11.880 --> 00:16:14.220
You must break your curse
by spring at the latest.

00:16:14.220 --> 00:16:17.640
If you cannot, then I shall
make Walter the heir.

00:16:17.640 --> 00:16:18.470
Is that clear?

00:16:18.470 --> 00:16:22.270
Yes. I'll take care of it
by spring at the latest.

00:16:22.270 --> 00:16:24.150
That is all I have to say.

00:16:24.150 --> 00:16:26.520
You may go home when you're done eating.

00:16:26.520 --> 00:16:30.820
Mother, I also have something
I'd like to discuss.

00:16:30.820 --> 00:16:32.280
What is it?

00:16:32.280 --> 00:16:35.450
It concerns Alice, the maid at the villa.

00:16:35.450 --> 00:16:38.700
She's here with me today.

00:16:38.700 --> 00:16:40.160
I met her last night.

00:16:40.160 --> 00:16:43.830
She's a lovely girl just like Sharon...
her mother.

00:16:43.830 --> 00:16:45.380
D-Darn straight!

00:16:46.960 --> 00:16:49.710
Oh, um... excuse me.

00:16:49.710 --> 00:16:53.050
I often talked with her mother.

00:16:53.050 --> 00:16:57.300
She was a wonderful person,
always smiling and cheerful.

00:16:57.300 --> 00:16:59.970
I still miss her to this day.

00:16:59.970 --> 00:17:03.440
But unlike their looks, it appears their
personalities aren't so similar.

00:17:03.440 --> 00:17:06.940
I-I admit Alice is cool and reserved,
but she's a really great person.

00:17:06.940 --> 00:17:11.480
She's attractive and talented! She's got
cute little mannerisms! She's perfect!

00:17:11.480 --> 00:17:13.240
That fast-talking sounds so creepy!

00:17:13.240 --> 00:17:15.110
You like her, don't you?

00:17:15.110 --> 00:17:19.830
Y-Yeah... That's why I'd like
your approval, Mother.

00:17:19.830 --> 00:17:24.370
Although we come from different classes,
one day I hope that Alice and I can--

00:17:24.370 --> 00:17:26.290
You've got to be joking.

00:17:26.290 --> 00:17:30.170
You're still a possible heir
to the family's title.

00:17:30.170 --> 00:17:31.880
Stop talking such nonsense...

00:17:31.880 --> 00:17:34.590
...and just think of a way
to break your curse.

00:17:34.590 --> 00:17:39.600
Since you were born into the aristocracy,
you aren't free to love whoever you wish.

00:17:39.600 --> 00:17:42.680
Particularly not a lowly maid.

00:17:42.680 --> 00:17:44.810
Even jokes have their lim--

00:17:44.810 --> 00:17:46.850
This is no...

00:17:46.850 --> 00:17:47.850
...joke!

00:17:49.270 --> 00:17:51.070
I'm totally serious.

00:17:51.070 --> 00:17:55.570
Who could joke about something like
this or speak of it half-heartedly?

00:17:55.570 --> 00:17:57.360
You locked me away in the villa,

00:17:57.360 --> 00:18:00.330
and since then, you've never
even tried getting to know me,

00:18:00.330 --> 00:18:03.580
but you're going to shackle my emotions?

00:18:03.580 --> 00:18:07.540
You won't even approve
of me loving Alice?!

00:18:07.540 --> 00:18:11.710
Alice always acts as though she
couldn't care less about my curse!

00:18:11.710 --> 00:18:15.130
She treats me like a normal human being!

00:18:15.130 --> 00:18:17.130
One's class and lineage...

00:18:17.130 --> 00:18:19.930
None of that matters!

00:18:19.930 --> 00:18:24.270
The one who saved me from the miserable
darkness that engulfed me was Alice!

00:18:25.180 --> 00:18:29.440
If it wasn't for Alice,
I'd be long since dead!

00:18:29.440 --> 00:18:32.320
Stop thinking only about
the family and heirs...

00:18:32.320 --> 00:18:36.280
...and spend a little time
thinking of your children!

00:18:36.280 --> 00:18:37.990
I...

00:18:37.990 --> 00:18:40.740
I'm marrying Alice!

00:18:47.250 --> 00:18:51.790
Walter, Viola, and I are not
your things, Mother.

00:18:55.050 --> 00:18:57.340
I-I'm leaving.

00:18:57.340 --> 00:19:00.890
Wait, Dearest Brother.
I'll see you to the door.

00:19:00.890 --> 00:19:01.930
Me, too.

00:19:06.930 --> 00:19:08.310
Madam?

00:19:08.310 --> 00:19:09.560
Leave them be.

00:19:13.770 --> 00:19:17.400
That boy, once so gentle and meek,

00:19:17.400 --> 00:19:19.570
actually had the nerve to talk back to me.

00:19:21.200 --> 00:19:22.780
My, how he's grown...

00:19:30.420 --> 00:19:33.210
I wish I could've said
it more skillfully...

00:19:33.210 --> 00:19:34.340
You did fine.

00:19:34.340 --> 00:19:36.880
It came as a shock, but it was priceless.

00:19:38.420 --> 00:19:40.930
Is something the matter, Your Grace?

00:19:40.930 --> 00:19:43.010
Oh, it's nothing.

00:19:43.010 --> 00:19:46.560
It's just that I didn't care for
the dinner they served here...

00:19:46.560 --> 00:19:48.600
Oh, I see.

00:19:48.600 --> 00:19:52.190
Shall we head back to
your house, Your Grace?

00:19:52.190 --> 00:19:55.360
Yeah, let's go. Back to our house.

00:19:55.360 --> 00:19:56.400
Yes, Your Grace.

00:21:13.140 --> 00:21:16.270
So, the reason the lady of
the house summoned you...

00:21:16.270 --> 00:21:19.940
...was to tell you to break your
curse by spring at the latest?

00:21:19.940 --> 00:21:23.990
Yeah, and if I can't,
then Walter inherits the family title.

00:21:23.990 --> 00:21:25.780
She made it very clear.

00:21:25.780 --> 00:21:27.700
I see.

00:21:27.700 --> 00:21:32.120
Well then, since I've gotten rid of all
my cards, I shall turn in for the night.

00:21:32.120 --> 00:21:35.170
Okay, Rob. Thanks for watching
the house while we were gone.

00:21:35.170 --> 00:21:36.920
Get some well-deserved rest.

00:21:36.920 --> 00:21:38.750
So, what would you like to do, Your Grace?

00:21:38.750 --> 00:21:40.880
Would you like to play some more cards?

00:21:40.880 --> 00:21:46.130
Well, if just the two of us play Old Maid,
we'll know where all the cards are...

00:21:46.130 --> 00:21:47.970
Then, what about a different
form of amusement?

00:21:47.970 --> 00:21:50.430
Cards! I want to play cards!

00:21:54.600 --> 00:21:56.730
The truth is I told Mother...

00:21:56.730 --> 00:21:59.110
...that I love you.

00:22:00.770 --> 00:22:03.570
And what did she say to that?

00:22:03.570 --> 00:22:05.650
Nothing, really...

00:22:05.650 --> 00:22:08.110
But I don't regret it.

00:22:08.110 --> 00:22:10.370
It's something I would've had
to tell her at some point.

00:22:11.580 --> 00:22:13.240
Because regardless of...

00:22:13.240 --> 00:22:16.330
...class or position,

00:22:16.330 --> 00:22:18.540
I love you...

00:22:23.460 --> 00:22:25.510
Pick a card.

00:22:25.510 --> 00:22:28.800
If you pick the king,
you'll win, Your Grace.

00:22:28.800 --> 00:22:31.640
"Both" is not an option.

00:22:37.890 --> 00:22:39.480
You win, Your Grace.

00:22:42.230 --> 00:22:43.820
This is how it should be.

00:22:43.820 --> 00:22:44.900
No, it's not!

00:22:47.780 --> 00:22:48.990
You taught me...

00:22:50.990 --> 00:22:53.080
...all sorts of things.

00:22:53.080 --> 00:22:55.290
You taught me how to love someone.

00:22:56.750 --> 00:22:58.670
I promise you this.

00:22:58.670 --> 00:23:00.170
I...

00:23:00.170 --> 00:23:03.340
...will give my love to you
now and always.

00:23:35.660 --> 00:23:36.830
I love you...

00:23:38.830 --> 00:23:40.170
...Your Grace.

00:23:47.170 --> 00:23:50.930
"We Want to Touch but We Can't--"

00:23:51.010 --> 00:23:52.970
"The Duke and Alice's..."

00:23:52.970 --> 00:23:55.010
"...Romance and Destiny..."

00:23:56.010 --> 00:23:58.220
"...Is Only Beginning--"
